191 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 149 0 R
/E (Retail banking customers frequently need information about banking products, loan eligibility, interest rates, fees, required documents, and banking procedures. Obtaining this information through traditional channels, such as bank branches and customer service hotlines, can involve waiting times, limited availability, and repetitive interactions.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
192 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 149 0 R
/E (This creates additional workload for customer support teams, particularly when they repeatedly handle routine questions that could be answered using existing banking documentation.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
193 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 149 0 R
/E (Furthermore, customers may experience difficulty finding accurate and up-to-date information across different documents and sources. This challenge can be more significant for customers who prefer communicating in Arabic or using natural language rather than searching through formal banking documents.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
194 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 149 0 R
/E (For Banque Misr, these challenges create an opportunity to improve customer access to banking information through an intelligent, automated assistant.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
195 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 149 0 R
/E (BankWise AI addresses this problem by developing AI-powered virtual banking assistant that provides customers with accessible and reliable banking information. The system combines Retrieval-Augmented Generation \(RAG\) to retrieve information from verified banking documents with deterministic rule-based calculations for financial operations such as car-loan eligibility and installment estimation.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
196 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 149 0 R
/E (Unlike a general-purpose chatbot, BankWise AI is designed to ground its responses in approved banking information and isolate financial calculations from generative AI to reduce incorrect answers and numerical hallucinations.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
197 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 149 0 R
/T (1.2 Project Objectives)
/E (1.2 Project Objectives)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
198 0 obj
<<
